<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6231"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 7:08 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK: &#39;the monster, he play the game to his liking&#39;? Your lust is like the craving of saltwater by a man dying of thirst. Clearly you are ahead of the game now, but you cannot win. Whatever victory you perceive will be very hollow and very lonely. With Valentine&#39;s Day approaching, does the monster say &#39;will you be mine?&#39; and hold you closely, kissing away your tears? Arms of monsters are always cold, just like the bodies of your victims. In many ways, you are their victim. They have you, and will not let you go. <BR>Your freedom of choice has been eroded away. Only prison awaits: man made or self made bars are bars nonetheless. <BR> <BR>Though the nature-nurture theory has been debated, one does follow in the steps of their biological line. Or to put it another way, the mistakes of your ancestors pursue you until you perish or decide otherwise. Even they are dead, and you are still in their grasp as well. <BR> <BR>&#34;Vampire of mine own heart; meanwhile a derelict. I am of those doomed to eternal laughter&#39;s throes, yet powerless to frame a smile.&#34; Baudelaire. <BR> <BR>If you want to read the ultimate poem, written by someone much like you, read the &#39;Hound of Heaven&#39;. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
