<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7433"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Micaela<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Micaela<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 15, 2005 - 11:26 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->To BTK: <BR> <BR>The Devil went down to Goergia one day, looking for a sack for his trash. He&#39;d used up so much copy paper trying to compose his witty rhymes.  <BR>Well, he found that trash sack and much much more. Near the Pacific was so much water, sand and bones. Bones! Can you belive it? <BR>He had some rope from Goergia so he tied the bones real nice. And took them back to his hotel and boiled them until the char rose and the bones were tender. <BR>He took the char and dried it out and made some warrior paint. He put the paint on his face and went to the nearest toy store to deprive them of that one special die cast mold train he had wanted for years. <BR>While he was driving home, he began to sneeze and realized he was allergic to the char. But thank GOD for Georgia kleenexes! So soft and redaily available. <BR>He got home and wiped his face with Northern papertowels. He finished his day sitting before the fire, counting his bones, admiring his train and wishing everyplace was like Georgia. <BR>Right before he went to bed, he pulled the venetian blind down. As he rolled over in his bed and began to drift of to sleep, the hair on the back of his neck stood up. <BR>He thought he heard a siren and his heart began racing. But alas, it was just the sad sweet voice of Ray Charles singing, &#34;Georgia On My Mind&#34;. He smiled and fell dreamlesly asleep. <BR> <BR>Alice7<!--/Text--></td></tr>
